'''G1 Climax 2026 Final''' was the concluding show of the [[G1 Climax 2026]] tournament produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on October 18, 2026 at the [[Aizawa Dome]] in [[Aizawa, Aizawa|Aizawa]], [[Aizawa Prefecture]]. The event was headlined by the tournament final between Block A winner [[Marcus Vance|Marcus "The Drill" Vance]] and Block B winner [[Taumafa Vaiahi|Taumafa]], with the winner earning an [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]] match against [[Leoni Masua]] at [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]] on January 4 at the [[Toyozawa Dome]].

Vance defeated Taumafa to win the G1 Climax, then spoke for the first time in his NOPW career to challenge Leoni Masua. The show also featured four championship matches, the [[KAZUKI (wrestler)|KAZUKI]]–[[Daigo Kuroki]] semi-main event, and a crowd of 30,000 — a sellout and the largest attendance of the 2026 tour.

== Background ==

Vance won Block A with the first perfect block in G1 history — 8-0-1, 17 points, the only blemish a 30-minute draw with the champion Leoni Masua in Naruto — and did it without speaking a single word on camera, a silence that became the tournament's central mystery. Taumafa won Block B in the first playoff in G1 history, defeating [[Takagi Yuto]] in Toyozawa on October 10 after both men finished the block stage at 7-2.

The contrast sold out the Aizawa Dome in six hours: the silent Mercian workhorse against the Vaiahi family's giant; the Drill Driver against the Samoan driver; the man who never lost against the man who learned how to. Vance made no appearances during the build — including the go-home contract signing at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 10|Episode 10]], where his chair sat empty beside the champion — while Taumafa and the family carried the promotion week.

