== Match details ==

* '''Match 1: Seigigun (Ono & Iwata) def. Cannon Club (Diallo & Tanaka).''' The Dome opener — the young lions against the Cannon Club's muscle. Diallo's power controlled the middle stretch until Iwata's hot tag turned it; the Ono Driver put Tanaka away at 10:24. '''Crowd:''' '''ONO''' chants. Big POP for the finish — the Dome warming up.
* '''Match 2: Nakamura & El Phantasma (c) def. Sato & Kimura.''' The Cannon Club's juniors retained, but the CHAOS challengers took them to the limit — Kimura's tope con giro wiped out the champions at ringside, and Sato's Prince's Landing nearly ended it at 12. The finish came off the scramble: Nakamura cut Kimura's springboard short and hit the Flash Flood for the pin at 13:37. '''Crowd:''' dueling chants. HEAT for the Flash's celebration. Respect applause for the challengers.
* '''Match 3: Koji Endo (c) def. Ryohei Maeda.''' The junior title match, and the match of the undercard. Maeda's speed against Endo's completeness — the Speed Star Press at 16:40 looked like the finish until Endo rolled through the impact and turned it into a small package for the three at 17:05. The champion retains by inches. Handshake after the bell. '''Crowd:''' '''SPEED STAR''' chants. ERUPTION for the counter. STANDING OVATION for both men.
* '''Match 4: Jusuf def. Reyes.''' The two men nobody would team with, alone in a Dome. Reyes brought the fight that made him the tournament's spoiler — the Cobra Twist sunk in at nine minutes — but Jusuf's mosaraza treated the Cobra's body as a map: the kneebar at 11:48, and when Reyes refused to tap, the referee stopped it. Jusuf left without acknowledgment, as always. Reyes stood, arm dangling, and bowed to the Dome. '''Crowd:''' silence for the stoppage. '''COBRA''' chants and a standing ovation for the loser. HEAT for Jusuf's exit.
* '''Match 5: Ishida (c) def. Honda.''' The television title — Ishida's mat game against Honda's Asikyran traditional wrestling, and the toughest test of the champion's run. Honda's throws and clinch work controlled long stretches; the champion's answer was patience and the leg. The Ishida Lock at 14:56 — Honda's seventh man to tap to it since the G1 began. Handshake and bow after, the AOPW ace's head high. '''Crowd:''' '''ISHIDA''' chants. Respect applause for Honda.
* '''Match 6: CHAOS (c) def. Cannon Club.''' The 6-man titles, and the Cannon Club's collapse played out on the Dome stage. Kengo wrestled five minutes of cheap shots and walked — stepped off the apron at 15, waved the Usos off, and left up the ramp. Tama and Riku fought on two-on-three; the numbers told at 18:29 when Kawada's Gamengiri put Riku down for the pin. CHAOS retains. The Usos left without their leader, without the match, and without answers. '''Crowd:''' NUCLEAR HEAT for Kengo's walk-out. '''CHAOS''' chants. Sympathy swell for the Usos.
* '''Match 7: KAZUKI def. Kuroki.''' The Kuroshio grudge, the Day 8 rematch, and the semi-main the Dome wanted. Strong style against artistry — Kuroki's forearms and the Black Iron Bomb (kicked out at 2.8) against the Twin Star Press (Kuroki rolled through the first at 17). The finish: the second Twin Star Press at 21:07, clean in the center. Then the moment — Kuroki rose, faced his brother, and bowed, both hands, the old gesture. KAZUKI stood still for a long second — and returned it. '''Crowd:''' '''KAZUKI''' / '''KUROKI''' dueling chants throughout. ERUPTION for the bow. STANDING OVATION.
* '''G1 Final: Vance def. Taumafa.''' The Workhorse against the giant, for the tournament and for the champion. Taumafa owned the first ten minutes — the power, the hip attack, the corner splash that folded Vance in half — before Vance went to the knee, the Ishida blueprint from Day 1 made explicit, and turned the giant's base into the story of the match. The exchange of miracles came late: Vance's Drill Driver at 22:00 — and Taumafa kicked out at 2.9, the first man to survive it all tour. The building came apart. Taumafa's Samoan driver at 25:30 — and Vance kicked out at 2.9, the first man to survive it at all. The Dome shook. Taumafa went for the second driver at 27 — Vance slid off the shoulder, 44 Calibre lariat, second Drill Driver — one, two, three at 27:44. '''Marcus Vance wins the G1 Climax 2026.''' '''Crowd:''' ERUPTION at both kickouts. '''THIS IS WRESTLING''' at 26. STANDING OVATION at the bell — and '''TAUMAFA''' chants for the giant, who bowed to the four corners before he left.

== Post-match: The Workhorse speaks ==

The trophy presentation ran its course — and then Marcus Vance, nine matches and seventeen points into the loudest silent run in NOPW history, took a microphone for the first time in his career. The Dome went quiet enough to hear the ring mic hum.

''"Seventeen points. No words. One more man."''

He pointed at the hard camera. The challenge made, he set the microphone down — and [[Leoni Masua]]'s music hit. The champion walked the ramp with the [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]] on his shoulder and the namo in his hand, stepped into the ring, and stood face to face with the winner. He said nothing back. The staredown closed the broadcast over the graphic: '''[[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]] — January 4 — [[Toyozawa Dome]].'''

'''Crowd:''' deafening silence during the promo — then an explosion. '''VANCE''' chants. MEGA POP for Leoni's music. The building on its feet for the staredown.

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The Workhorse speaks.''' Nine matches, 8-0-1 in the block, the perfect tournament — and when the silence finally broke it broke in seven words. Vance challenges [[Leoni Masua]] at Wrestling Summit: the Drill against the Spear, the workhorse against the chief, the man who never talked against the man who never stopped.
* '''The giant loses nothing.''' Taumafa kicked out of the Drill Driver — the first man to do it — and took the champion's challenger to 27:44. The family's G1 ends in defeat, but the Dome chanted his name leaving.
* '''The bow returned.''' KAZUKI and Kuroki settled the grudge the way Kuroshio settled everything — clean, in the center, with the old gesture. Both men move to Summit season whole.
* '''The collapse is on camera now.''' Kengo walked out on the Usos at the Aizawa Dome. The Cannon Club leaves the G1 season with its juniors' gold — and a leader who abandons his own family in title matches.
* '''Ishida's number.''' Seven submissions since the G1 began, the 8:56 reclaimed at Episode 10, and the television title defended at the Dome. The block's best story kept writing itself.

